    <bpmn:process id="W_W1206" name="W1206. AI-Powered Demand Forecasting Model Training, Accuracy Monitoring &amp; Retraining Cycle" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled monthly model performance review; or triggered by forecast accuracy degradation below threshold
Frequency: Monthly accuracy monitoring; quarterly model retraining; annual full model rebuild
Volume: Forecasting engine generates predictions for 35,000 active SKUs across ~204 locations (200 stores + 4 DCs) = ~7.14M SKU-location forecasts per planning cycle
Owner: Data Science Lead
Participants: Data Science Lead, Supply Planner, Category Manager, IT Data Engineer, VP Merchandising (model governance)
Source: workflow W1206 — AI-Powered Demand Forecasting Model Training, Accuracy Monitoring &amp; Retraining Cycle</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1206_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1206_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1206_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1206_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1206_Lane2" name="Data Science Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1206_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1206_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1206_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1206_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1206_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1206_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1206_Start4" name="Scheduled monthly model performance review; or triggered by forecast accuracy degradation…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1206_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1206_Task5" name="Monthly accuracy monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly accuracy monitoring: System calculates forecast accuracy metrics for the past month: (a) MAPE (Mean Absolute Percentage Error) by SKU category, by store cluster, by DC, (b) WAPE (Weighted Absolute Percentage Error) for revenue-weighted accuracy, (c) bias (systematic over-forecast vs. under-forecast), (d) accuracy by lead time bucket (7-day, 14-day, 30-day forecast horizons), (e) exception report: SKUs where MAPE &gt; 40% or bias &gt; ±20%; Data Science Lead reviews dashboard and identifies accuracy degradation trends
Responsible (R): System / Data Science Lead
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1206_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1206_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1206_Task6" name="Root cause analysis for degradation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Root cause analysis for degradation: When accuracy degrades below threshold (MAPE &gt; 35% for category, or &gt; 40% for individual SKU clusters): Data Science Lead investigates: (a) data quality issues (missing POS transactions from offline stores, late GR postings, incorrect item master data), (b) concept drift (demand pattern changed due to new competitor store opening, infrastructure project, or seasonal anomaly), (c) feature drift (input variables no longer predictive — e.g., weather data source changed), (d) model staleness (model not retrained with recent data); documents findings in model performance log
Responsible (R): Data Science Lead
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 4–8 hours/analysis</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1206_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1206_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1206_Task7" name="Quarterly model retraining">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quarterly model retraining: Every quarter: Data Science Lead executes model retraining pipeline: (a) extracts latest 24 months of cleaned demand data (POS transactions, replenishment orders, ecommerce orders), (b) updates feature engineering pipeline: (i) calendar features (holidays, paydays, school calendar), (ii) weather features (PAGASA rainfall, temperature data), (iii) promotional features (sale events, markdown calendar), (iv) external features (construction permits, LGU infrastructure projects), (c) retrains model ensemble (time-series models + gradient boosting + neural network blend) on updated data, (d) validates on holdout period (most recent 3 months), (e) compares new model accuracy vs. production model; clears the holdout gate (&gt; 2% WAPE improvement) for champion-challenger validation (Step 4)
Responsible (R): Data Science Lead / IT Data Engineer
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 20–30 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1206_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1206_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1206_Task8" name="Champion-challenger validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Champion-challenger validation: Before promoting retrained model to production: (a) run champion (current production model) and challenger (newly trained model) in parallel for 2 weeks, (b) compare forecast accuracy and bias side-by-side on identical SKU-location forecasts, (c) if challenger wins: promote to production with automated rollback capability if accuracy drops in first week, (d) if champion wins: retain current model and investigate challenger weaknesses for next training cycle
Responsible (R): Data Science Lead
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/quarter (after automated parallel run)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1206_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1206_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1206_Task9" name="Annual full model rebuild">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual full model rebuild: Once a year: Data Science Lead conducts comprehensive model review: (a) evaluates whether current model architecture is still optimal (e.g., evaluate new transformer-based models, evaluate external data sources), (b) benchmarks BuildRight&#x27;s forecast accuracy against retail industry benchmarks (target: MAPE &lt; 25% at category level, &lt; 35% at SKU level), (c) evaluates new features and data sources (e.g., foot traffic data, social media sentiment, competitor pricing), (d) if warranted, rebuilds model with updated architecture and features, (e) presents model performance report and improvement roadmap to VP Merchandising and CIO
Responsible (R): Data Science Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 40–60 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1206_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1206_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1206_Task10" name="Model governance and documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Model governance and documentation: Data Science Lead maintains model governance documentation: (a) model card describing purpose, inputs, outputs, accuracy, limitations, (b) data lineage documentation (what data feeds the model, where it comes from, how it&#x27;s cleaned), (c) model change log (every retraining, every feature change, every architecture update), (d) bias and fairness assessment (does the model systematically over/under-forecast for specific store types or regions), (e) compliance with BuildRight&#x27;s AI governance policy per W689; documentation reviewed by VP Merchandising semi-annually
Responsible (R): Data Science Lead
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1206_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1206_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1206_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1206_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1206_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-223 (ensure responsible AI/ML &amp; pilot governance.) | - operational: annual architecture review in Step 5 and evaluation of new external data sources; operational: data quality pipeline in Step 2 and data governance per W1177; operational: 24-month training window and holdout validation in Step 3
Owner: Data Science Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1206_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1206_Annotation12" targetRef="W1206_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
