    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1339" name="W1339. Computer Vision-Based Shelf Audit &amp; Planogram Compliance Monitoring" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — weekly shelf audit cycle per store; or triggered by planogram compliance score drop below 80%; or new planogram deployment requiring compliance validation
Frequency: Weekly automated shelf audit for top-50 planogram categories; monthly full-store audit; quarterly model retraining
Volume: 200 stores × 12 major categories × weekly audit = ~2,400 category-level audits/week; top-50 high-priority planograms audited monthly (10,000/month, phased 2,500/week); remaining planograms audited monthly
Owner: Data Science Lead
Participants: BI Analyst, Category Manager, Store Manager, Visual Merchandising Coordinator, IT Data Engineer
Source: workflow W1339 — Computer Vision-Based Shelf Audit &amp; Planogram Compliance Monitoring</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1339_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1339_Lane1" name="Store Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1339_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1339_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1339_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1339_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1339_Lane3" name="BI Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1339_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1339_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1339_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1339_Lane5" name="Data Science Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1339_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1339_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1339_Start7" name="Scheduled — weekly shelf audit cycle per store; or triggered by planogram compliance…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1339_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1339_Task8" name="Image capture">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Image capture: Store associates capture shelf images using mobile app during daily walkthrough (W5A): (a) dedicated shelf audit module in store operations app: select category → capture 3–5 images of shelf section covering the full planogram area, (b) images tagged with store ID, category, shelf section, date/time, and associate ID, (c) capture protocol: images must cover full shelf width and height, adequate lighting (use flash in dim areas), minimal blur (steady hand or elbow brace), (d) for pilot stores (10 stores): fixed overhead cameras capture daily images of high-priority categories (power tools, paint wall, tile gallery)
Responsible (R): Store Associate
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min/category</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1339_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1339_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1339_Task9" name="Computer vision inference">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Computer vision inference: AI model processes captured images: (a) product detection: identify individual products on shelf using object detection model trained on BuildRight&#x27;s product image library (35,000 SKUs with images from W50), (b) shelf position mapping: map detected products to planogram positions (which product should be where per planogram definition in space planning module), (c) compliance scoring per shelf section: (i) correct product in correct position (% compliance), (ii) out-of-stock positions (empty shelf where product should be), (iii) facing count: correct number of product facings vs. planogram, (iv) misplaced products: products in wrong position, (v) missing price labels, (d) generate compliance report per category per store with visual overlay showing detected issues on shelf image
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (&lt; 30 sec/image)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1339_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1339_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1339_Task10" name="Exception triage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Exception triage: BI Analyst reviews compliance exceptions flagged by computer vision: (a) categories with compliance &lt; 80% escalated to Store Manager for immediate correction, (b) recurring out-of-stock positions flagged for replenishment review per W4 (is replenishment failing or is demand exceeding forecast?), (c) persistent misplacement patterns flagged for Category Manager — is the planogram unrealistic for the physical shelf configuration?, (d) false positive review: BI Analyst samples 5% of AI-flagged issues and compares to actual shelf condition — is the model making accurate detections?
Responsible (R): BI Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1339_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1339_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1339_Task11" name="Store Manager compliance workflow">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Store Manager compliance workflow: Store Manager receives weekly compliance report via store operations app: (a) list of non-compliant shelf positions with AI-generated visual overlay showing what&#x27;s wrong, (b) corrective action: Store Associate repositions products per planogram, (c) Store Associate captures follow-up image after correction, (d) system re-runs inference to confirm correction, (e) compliance improvement tracked week-over-week per store, (f) store compliance score feeds into store performance scorecard per W1214
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Store Associate
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 15–30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1339_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1339_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1339_Task12" name="Model performance monitoring &amp; retraining">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Model performance monitoring &amp; retraining: Data Science Lead monitors computer vision model performance: (a) track accuracy: precision and recall of product detection, false positive rate for out-of-stock detection, facing count accuracy, (b) quarterly: retrain model with new product images from W50 (new SKUs added to assortment) and corrected annotations from BI Analyst false positive review, (c) evaluate new model version vs. production model — promote only if accuracy improvement &gt; 2%, (d) monitor for seasonal challenges: Christmas decorations in store may confuse model, planogram resets introduce new configurations
Responsible (R): Data Science Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1339_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1339_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1339_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1339_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1339_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-332 (ensure controlled execution — AI/ML &amp; Automation (PA-30.2).) | - operational: in-app capture-protocol and image-quality gating at capture time; operational: model retraining gated on annotated false-positive review with version-promotion threshold &gt;2% accuracy improvement; operational: capture scope capped to the audited planogram set with Store Manager visibility of results
Owner: Data Science Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1339_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1339_Annotation14" targetRef="W1339_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
