    <bpmn:process id="W_W1340" name="W1340. Conversational AI Customer Service Chatbot Lifecycle Management &amp; Escalation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer initiates chat on BuildRight website, mobile app, or Facebook Messenger; or escalation from chatbot to human agent
Frequency: ~15,000–20,000 chat interactions/month; ~60% resolved by chatbot without human intervention
Volume: ~180,000–240,000 chat interactions/year; ~108,000–144,000 automated resolutions/year
Owner: Digital Commerce Manager
Participants: Customer Service Agent (escalation), Data Science Lead (NLP model), Content Specialist (knowledge base), IT Operations (platform), Marketing (conversation design)
Source: workflow W1340 — Conversational AI Customer Service Chatbot Lifecycle Management &amp; Escalation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1340_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1340_Lane1" name="Content Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1340_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1340_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1340_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1340_Lane2" name="Data Science Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1340_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1340_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1340_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1340_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1340_Lane4" name="Digital Commerce Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1340_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1340_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1340_Start6" name="Customer initiates chat on BuildRight website, mobile app, or Facebook Messenger; or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1340_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1340_Task7" name="Conversation design &amp; intent mapping">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Conversation design &amp; intent mapping: Content Specialist and Digital Commerce Manager design chatbot conversation flows: (a) identify top-20 customer intents from historical customer service ticket analysis: product availability, pricing inquiry, order status, return policy, store hours/location, installation booking, loyalty points inquiry, payment options, delivery tracking, complaint, product recommendation, B2B credit application, promo inquiry, bulk order, warranty claim, tool rental availability, cutting service request, gift card balance, career inquiry, (b) design conversation flow per intent: greeting → intent identification → information gathering → response/action → satisfaction check → closing, (c) design fallback: &quot;I&#x27;m sorry, I can&#x27;t help with that. Let me connect you to a team member.&quot; with warm handoff to human agent per W13, (d) design persona: BuildRight brand voice — helpful, knowledgeable, &quot;kuya/ate&quot; warmth appropriate for Filipino customer base
Responsible (R): Content Specialist / Digital Commerce Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 10–15 days (initial design)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1340_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1340_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1340_Task8" name="Knowledge base development">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Knowledge base development: Content Specialist populates chatbot knowledge base: (a) product FAQ database: 200+ questions covering common product inquiries (What&#x27;s the difference between PVC and GI pipe? How many tiles do I need for a 20 sqm bathroom? Which paint for exterior walls?), (b) store information database: location, hours, services, contact numbers for all 200 stores, (c) policy database: return policy, warranty terms, delivery terms, installation service terms, loyalty program rules, (d) pricing integration: chatbot queries real-time pricing from ERP for specific SKU inquiries, (e) availability integration: chatbot queries real-time stock from inventory module for store-level availability, (f) Taglish support: train NLP model on Filipino English (Taglish) expressions common in Philippine customer queries (&quot;Meron ba kayong cement na Portland type sa Cagayan de Oro branch?&quot;)
Responsible (R): Content Specialist / IT Data Engineer
Accountable (A): Digital Commerce Manager
Duration: 5–10 days (initial) + ongoing maintenance</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1340_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1340_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1340_Task9" name="NLP model training &amp; deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: NLP model training &amp; deployment: Data Science Lead trains and deploys the conversational AI model: (a) train intent classification model on annotated customer query dataset: Tagalog, English, and Taglish variations for each intent, (b) train entity extraction model: extract product names, store locations, order numbers, dates from customer messages, (c) integrate with backend systems: product availability API, order tracking API, loyalty points API, store locator API, (d) deploy to channels: website chat widget, mobile app SDK, Facebook Messenger integration via Messenger Platform API, Viber chat extension, (e) A/B test chatbot vs. current live-chat flow for 2 weeks before full deployment
Responsible (R): Data Science Lead / IT Operations
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 3–4 weeks (initial)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1340_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1340_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1340_Task10" name="Human agent escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Human agent escalation: When chatbot cannot resolve: (a) chatbot performs warm handoff to human agent per W13: transfers conversation transcript, customer profile, and chatbot&#x27;s attempted resolution to agent console, (b) human agent sees full conversation history and continues seamlessly — customer does not need to repeat information, (c) escalation triggers: (i) customer explicitly requests human agent, (ii) chatbot fails to identify intent after 2 attempts, (iii) sentiment analysis detects customer frustration (negative keywords in Filipino: &quot;nakakainis,&quot; &quot;bulok,&quot; &quot;walang kwenta&quot;), (iv) inquiry involves complaint, safety concern, or B2B negotiation requiring human judgment, (d) target: human agent response within 2 minutes of escalation during business hours
Responsible (R): System / Customer Service Agent
Accountable (A): Customer Service Manager
Duration: Per interaction</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1340_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1340_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1340_Task11" name="Continuous monitoring &amp; improvement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Continuous monitoring &amp; improvement: Digital Commerce Manager reviews chatbot performance weekly: (a) Resolution rate: % of interactions resolved by chatbot without escalation — target 60%+, (b) Intent accuracy: % of correctly identified customer intents — target 85%+, (c) Customer satisfaction: post-chat CSAT survey (1–5 scale) — target 4.0+ for chatbot interactions, (d) Escalation analysis: which intents most frequently escalate? — prioritize knowledge base improvement for these intents, (e) New intent discovery: review unresolved queries for emerging intents not in current model — add to training data, (f) Channel performance: compare resolution rate across website, app, Messenger, and Viber
Responsible (R): Digital Commerce Manager / Data Science Lead
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2–3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1340_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1340_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1340_Task12" name="Quarterly model retraining">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly model retraining: Data Science Lead retrains NLP model quarterly: (a) incorporate new conversation logs (with customer PII removed per RA 10173), (b) add new intents and Taglish expressions identified in monitoring, (c) update knowledge base with new product information per W50, (d) retrain and validate: compare new model accuracy to production model, (e) deploy updated model if accuracy improvement &gt; 1%
Responsible (R): Data Science Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 8–12 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1340_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1340_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1340_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1340_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1340_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-332 (ensure controlled execution — AI/ML &amp; Automation (PA-30.2).) | - operational: building a custom Taglish training dataset from BuildRight&#x27;s customer interaction history; operational: prominent &quot;Talk to a person&quot; option and warm handoff with no information loss; operational: real-time API integration for pricing and availability (not static knowledge base)
Owner: Digital Commerce Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1340_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1340_Annotation14" targetRef="W1340_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1340_Flow16" sourceRef="W1340_Start6" targetRef="W1340_Task7" />
