    <bpmn:process id="W_W1341" name="W1341. Intelligent Document Processing (IDP) for Invoice &amp; Receipt Automation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor invoice received via email, vendor portal, or mail; customer receipt presented for return (W12); or delivery receipt received at DC (W3)
Frequency: ~8,500–9,500 vendor invoices/month; ~1,200 return receipts/month (the ~40/day AR-credit-memo canon, ~0.04% of POS volume); ~6,000 DC delivery receipts/month (~6,500–6,600 incl. DSD; canon §15.1)
Volume: ~70,000–75,000 documents/month requiring data extraction across AP, returns, and receiving (per the Frequency itemization)
Owner: IT Business Analyst
Participants: AP Clerk, Data Science Lead, IT Developer, AP Supervisor, Finance Controller
Source: workflow W1341 — Intelligent Document Processing (IDP) for Invoice &amp; Receipt Automation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1341_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1341_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1341_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1341_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1341_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1341_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1341_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1341_Lane2" name="AP Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1341_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1341_Lane3" name="Data Science Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1341_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1341_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1341_Start5" name="Vendor invoice received via email, vendor portal, or mail; customer receipt presented for…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1341_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1341_Task6" name="Document intake &amp; classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Document intake &amp; classification: IDP system receives documents: (a) Vendor invoices: received via email (PDF attachments), vendor portal upload (W705), or scanned from mail — system classifies as invoice, credit note, or statement, (b) Return receipts: photographed at POS during return processing per W12 — system classifies as return receipt, (c) Delivery receipts: scanned at DC receiving per W3 — system classifies as delivery receipt (DR), packing list, or bill of lading; document type triggers appropriate extraction template
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (&lt; 5 sec/document)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1341_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1341_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1341_Task7" name="OCR &amp; data extraction">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: OCR &amp; data extraction: IDP engine extracts key fields: (a) Vendor invoices: vendor name (matched to vendor master), invoice number, invoice date, due date, line items (SKU description, quantity, unit price, amount), tax (VAT 12%), total amount, payment terms; for each field: confidence score (0–100%) generated, (b) Return receipts: transaction ID, date/time, store number, items returned, quantities, amounts, payment method, (c) Delivery receipts: vendor name, DR number, PO reference, items delivered, quantities, condition (good/damaged); extraction uses layout analysis + OCR + NLP to handle diverse Philippine document formats
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (&lt; 10 sec/document)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1341_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1341_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1341_Task8" name="Validation &amp; matching">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Validation &amp; matching: System validates extracted data against ERP: (a) Invoice validation: (i) vendor name matched to vendor master (fuzzy matching for name variations), (ii) PO number matched to open PO in procurement module, (iii) line item SKU matched to item master, (iv) quantity matched to goods receipt per W3 (three-way match per W7), (v) price matched to PO price — flag variances &gt; 1%, (vi) VAT calculation verified (12% per Philippine tax law), (b) Return receipt validation: (i) transaction ID matched to POS transaction log, (ii) items and quantities validated against transaction, (c) Delivery receipt validation: (i) PO number matched, (ii) quantities matched to PO quantities, (iii) over/under delivery flagged; documents with all validations passing routed for auto-processing; documents with validation failures routed for manual review
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): AP Clerk / AP Supervisor
Duration: Automated + exception handling</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1341_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1341_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1341_Task9" name="Exception handling &amp; manual review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Exception handling &amp; manual review: AP Clerk reviews documents with extraction or validation failures: (a) extraction confidence &lt; 80%: clerk manually verifies and corrects extracted fields, (b) vendor name not matched: clerk identifies correct vendor and links — system learns the name variation for future matching, (c) PO not matched: clerk investigates (wrong PO, missing PO, vendor error) and resolves per W7, (d) price variance: clerk investigates (price change, promotional pricing, vendor error) and resolves, (e) each correction feeds back to IDP model for continuous learning — model accuracy improves over time
Responsible (R): AP Clerk
Accountable (A): AP Supervisor
Duration: 2–5 min/exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1341_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1341_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1341_Task10" name="Straight-through processing (STP)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Straight-through processing (STP): Documents passing all validations: (a) system auto-creates AP invoice in ERP with extracted data, (b) system auto-matches to PO and GR (three-way match), (c) system auto-routes for approval based on amount threshold per W7, (d) STP target: 70% of vendor invoices processed without manual intervention within 12 months of deployment, (e) AP Supervisor monitors STP rate daily — target increasing monthly
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): AP Supervisor
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1341_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1341_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1341_Task11" name="Model performance monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Model performance monitoring: Data Science Lead monitors IDP model performance monthly: (a) extraction accuracy per field type: vendor name, invoice number, date, amount, line items — target &gt; 95% for key fields, (b) STP rate: % of documents fully automated — track trend, (c) false positive rate: % of auto-processed documents later found to have extraction errors — target &lt; 0.5%, (d) quarterly: retrain OCR and NLP models with corrected documents from exception handling — model accuracy improves with each retraining cycle, (e) evaluate new vendor invoice formats — when a new vendor is onboarded per W224, their invoice format is initially low-confidence; after ~10 manually reviewed invoices, the model learns the format
Responsible (R): Data Science Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4–8 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1341_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1341_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1341_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1341_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1341_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-332 (ensure controlled execution — AI/ML &amp; Automation (PA-30.2).) | - operational: layout-agnostic extraction and continuous learning from corrections; operational: routing documents with detected handwriting for manual review; operational: multi-language OCR configuration and routing non-English invoices for manual processing
Owner: IT Business Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1341_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1341_Annotation13" targetRef="W1341_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
