    <bpmn:process id="W_W1453" name="W1453. IoT-Enabled Shelf Monitoring, Real-Time Stock-Out Detection &amp; Automated Replenishment Trigger" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: IoT sensor deployment phase (piloting in 10 stores then expanding); continuous real-time monitoring once deployed
Frequency: Real-time sensor monitoring (24/7); weekly exception review; monthly accuracy validation against cycle counts
Volume: Pilot: 10 stores × ~3,500 shelf positions monitored per store = ~35,000 sensors; full deployment target: 200 stores × 3,500 = ~700,000 sensors (phased over 3 years)
Owner: CIO
Participants: CIO, IT IoT Engineer, Store Manager, Department Supervisor, Supply Planning Manager, BI Analytics Manager, External IoT Vendor
Source: workflow W1453 — IoT-Enabled Shelf Monitoring, Real-Time Stock-Out Detection &amp; Automated Replenishment Trigger</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1453_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1453_Lane1" name="IT IoT Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1453_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1453_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1453_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1453_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1453_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1453_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1453_Lane3" name="CIO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1453_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1453_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1453_Start5" name="IoT sensor deployment phase (piloting in 10 stores then expanding); continuous real-time…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1453_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1453_Task6" name="Pilot deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pilot deployment (10 stores, ~3,500 shelf positions each): (a) CIO selects pilot stores: 2 stores per region (Metro Manila, Luzon, Visayas, Mindanao, new market), (b) IT IoT Engineer works with external IoT vendor to: (i) install shelf weight sensors on top 3,500 SKUs by velocity, (ii) connect sensors to store gateway (Wi-Fi or LoRaWAN), (iii) configure threshold: sensor weight below X grams = stock-out alert, (iv) integrate sensor data with ERP inventory module, (c) calibrate sensors during first 2 weeks: compare sensor stock-out alerts with manual shelf checks — target ≥ 95% accuracy
Responsible (R): IT IoT Engineer / External Vendor
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 8–12 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1453_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1453_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1453_Task7" name="Real-time stock-out detection and alerting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Real-time stock-out detection and alerting: Once operational: (a) sensor detects weight below threshold → system generates stock-out alert within 5 minutes, (b) alert routed to: (i) Store Stock Associate mobile app: &quot;Aisle 3, Bay 7, Shelf 2: Cement (SKU 12345) — empty shelf detected. Please verify and replenish.&quot;, (ii) Store Manager dashboard: real-time stock-out map of store, (iii) BI dashboard: chain-wide stock-out rate for monitored SKUs, (c) Stock Associate acknowledges alert, physically verifies (sensor may false-trigger from misaligned product), and replenishes from backroom or triggers replenishment order from DC if backroom is also empty
Responsible (R): System (automated) / Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1453_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1453_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1453_Task8" name="Automated replenishment trigger">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Automated replenishment trigger: For verified stock-outs where backroom is also empty: (a) system automatically creates emergency replenishment order to DC: (i) item, quantity (standard case pack), priority flag (&quot;IoT-triggered — shelf empty&quot;), (ii) DC includes in next available delivery to the store, (b) for stores in the pilot: track &quot;IoT-triggered replenishment&quot; orders separately to measure impact on stock-out duration and lost sales reduction
Responsible (R): System / Supply Planning Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1453_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1453_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1453_Task9" name="Weekly accuracy validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Weekly accuracy validation: IT IoT Engineer and Store Manager conduct weekly accuracy review: (a) compare sensor stock-out alerts vs. manual shelf checks (random sample of 50 shelf positions/week), (b) calculate: (i) true positive rate (sensor correctly detected stock-out), (ii) false positive rate (sensor said empty but shelf was stocked), (iii) false negative rate (sensor said stocked but shelf was empty), (d) if accuracy &lt; 90%: recalibrate sensors, adjust weight thresholds, or address physical issues (products blocking sensors, sensor displacement), (e) monthly: compare IoT stock-out data with cycle count data per W276 for validation
Responsible (R): IT IoT Engineer
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4 hours/week during pilot</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1453_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1453_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1453_Task10" name="Pilot evaluation and expansion planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Pilot evaluation and expansion planning (after 6-month pilot): (a) CIO compiles pilot results: (i) stock-out detection speed improvement (from 4–8 hours to &lt; 5 min), (ii) stock-out rate reduction (target: 50% reduction in monitored SKU stock-outs), (iii) revenue impact (estimated sales recaptured from faster replenishment), (iv) sensor accuracy and reliability (target: ≥ 95%), (v) false positive rate and staff workload impact, (b) calculate ROI: (i) pilot cost (hardware + installation + maintenance) vs. (ii) revenue recaptured + operational efficiency gains, (c) if ROI positive: propose phased expansion plan to CEO — Year 1: 50 stores, Year 2: 100 stores, Year 3: all 200 stores, (d) present to CIO and COO for budget approval
Responsible (R): CIO
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1453_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1453_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1453_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1453_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1453_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-332 (ensure controlled execution — AI/ML &amp; Automation (PA-30.2).) | - operational: CIO review and approval gate
Owner: CIO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1453_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1453_Annotation12" targetRef="W1453_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1453_Flow14" sourceRef="W1453_Start5" targetRef="W1453_Task6" />
