        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1453_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1453_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1453_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1453_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1453_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1453_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1453_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1453_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1453_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1453_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1453_Flow19_di" bpmnElement="W1453_Flow19"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1453_Assoc13_di" bpmnElement="W1453_Assoc13"><di:waypoint x="340" y="630" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1454" name="W1454. Augmented Reality (AR) Home Visualization Tool Operations, 3D Product Catalog &amp; Customer Project Planning" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Product catalog update cycle (monthly); or AR feature request from marketing; or quarterly AR tool usage analytics review
Frequency: Monthly 3D model updates; quarterly feature enhancement; continuous customer usage monitoring
Volume: Initial launch: 500 top-selling SKUs with 3D models (tiles, paint, fixtures, appliances, furniture); target: 5,000 SKUs within 2 years; ~42,900 ecommerce orders/month as the potential AR-engaged order volume
Owner: CIO
Participants: CIO, E-Commerce Manager, Content Manager, 3D Modeler, Category Managers, Marketing Campaign Manager, External AR Development Partner
Source: workflow W1454 — Augmented Reality (AR) Home Visualization Tool Operations, 3D Product Catalog &amp; Customer Project Planning</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1454_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1454_Lane1" name="3D Modeler">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1454_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1454_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1454_Lane2" name="CIO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1454_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1454_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1454_Lane3" name="Content Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1454_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1454_Lane4" name="BI Analytics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1454_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1454_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1454_Start6" name="Product catalog update cycle (monthly); or AR feature request from marketing; or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1454_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1454_Task7" name="3D product model creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: 3D product model creation: 3D Modeler creates AR-ready 3D models for top-selling SKUs: (a) Category Managers prioritize SKU list: (i) Tiles: top 200 designs (high visual impact, easy to model as flat surfaces), (ii) Paint: all available colors as wall overlays (easier to model — color swatches applied to AR-detected wall planes), (iii) Fixtures: top 50 faucets, 30 light fixtures, 20 toilets (3D models with accurate dimensions), (iv) Appliances: top 30 fans, aircons, water heaters, (v) Furniture: top 20 shelving, storage units, (b) 3D Modeler produces: (i) high-fidelity 3D model (texture, material, dimensions), (ii) AR-optimized model (poly count &lt; 50K for mobile performance), (iii) metadata: actual dimensions, price, availability, related products, (c) models stored in 3D asset library integrated with PIM per W50
Responsible (R): 3D Modeler / Category Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–2 hours per model</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1454_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1454_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1454_Task8" name="AR app integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: AR app integration: CIO and External AR Partner integrate AR tool into BuildRight mobile app: (a) AR features: (i) &quot;Visualize in Your Space&quot; — customer points phone camera at floor/wall; system detects surface plane and places selected product at actual scale, (ii) &quot;Paint Your Room&quot; — customer scans room; system applies selected paint color to walls, (iii) &quot;Tile Your Floor&quot; — customer scans floor; system tiles the surface with selected tile pattern at actual tile size, (iv) &quot;Place Appliance&quot; — customer places virtual appliance in room to check fit and aesthetics, (b) capture screenshot/save feature: customer saves AR visualization and shares via social media or WhatsApp (drives viral marketing per W1443), (c) &quot;Buy This Look&quot; button: from AR visualization, customer adds all items in the scene to cart (cross-sell), (d) AR tool available on buildright.com.ph mobile app (iOS and Android)
Responsible (R): CIO / External AR Partner
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Initial: 3–4 months; Ongoing: 2 weeks per feature update</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1454_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1454_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1454_Task9" name="Monthly 3D catalog expansion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly 3D catalog expansion: Content Manager and 3D Modeler expand 3D catalog monthly: (a) add new SKUs from last month&#x27;s assortment updates (per W1), (b) update models for product changes (new tile sizes, fixture finishes), (c) prioritize based on: (i) sales velocity (top sellers get AR first), (ii) ecommerce page views (high-traffic products benefit most from AR), (iii) visual complexity (products where seeing in-context adds the most value), (d) target: add 100–200 new 3D models per month
Responsible (R): Content Manager / 3D Modeler
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 100–400 hours/month (1–2 h/model)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1454_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1454_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1454_Task10" name="Quarterly AR usage analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly AR usage analytics: BI Analytics Manager compiles AR tool analytics: (a) usage metrics: (i) AR sessions per month, (ii) unique users, (iii) average session duration, (iv) features used (visualize, paint, tile, place), (b) conversion metrics: (i) AR user conversion rate vs. non-AR user conversion rate, (ii) AR-influenced revenue (orders where AR was used before purchase), (iii) average order value: AR users vs. non-AR users, (c) engagement metrics: (i) screenshots shared, (ii) social media mentions of AR feature, (d) ROI: AR development and maintenance cost vs. incremental revenue from AR-influenced purchases
Responsible (R): BI Analytics Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1454_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1454_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1454_Task11" name="Annual AR strategy review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual AR strategy review: CIO and CMO review AR program: (a) year-over-year usage growth, (b) competitive landscape — have competitors launched AR features?, (c) technology advances — new AR capabilities (e.g., Apple Vision Pro, AR glasses), (d) budget for next year: model creation, platform maintenance, new features, (e) decide: (i) expand SKU coverage (5,000 → 10,000), (ii) add new AR features (e.g., full room design, project planning), (iii) deploy in-store AR (kiosks or associate tablets for customer assistance)
Responsible (R): CIO / CMO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1454_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1454_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1454_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1454_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1454_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-332 (ensure controlled execution — AI/ML &amp; Automation (PA-30.2).) | - operational: CIO review and approval gate
Owner: CIO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
