    <bpmn:process id="W_W1571" name="W1571. AI-Powered Vendor Negotiation Price Optimization, Cost Prediction &amp; Purchase Order Timing Recommendation Engine" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly vendor negotiation cycle per W738; or new vendor contract renewal approaching; or significant commodity price movement detected; or monthly procurement analytics review
Frequency: Quarterly model refresh; continuous price monitoring; recommendation generation per negotiation event
Volume: ~800–1,000 active vendors; ~200 vendors with annual contract negotiations; ~20 vendors (top by COGS) with quarterly price reviews
Owner: Senior Data Scientist
Participants: Senior Data Scientist, Category Manager, VP Merchandising, CFO, Procurement Manager
Source: workflow W1571 — AI-Powered Vendor Negotiation Price Optimization, Cost Prediction &amp; Purchase Order Timing Recommendation Engine</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1571_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1571_Lane1" name="Senior Data Scientist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1571_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1571_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1571_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1571_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1571_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1571_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1571_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1571_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1571_Start4" name="Quarterly vendor negotiation cycle per W738; or new vendor contract renewal approaching…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1571_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1571_Task5" name="Data collection &amp; integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Data collection &amp; integration: Senior Data Scientist integrates data sources: (a) historical purchase prices by vendor, SKU, and date (from ERP AP module); (b) commodity price feeds: global steel (LME), copper (LME), lumber (Random Lengths), oil (Brent), cement (Philippine wholesale index); (c) vendor performance data: on-time delivery rate, quality rejection rate, fill rate per W738; (d) foreign exchange rates (USD/PHP for imports); (e) Philippine inflation data (PSA); (f) seasonal demand patterns per W2 demand forecast
Responsible (R): Senior Data Scientist / Data Engineer
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 4–6 weeks (initial)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1571_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1571_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1571_Task6" name="Price prediction model development">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Price prediction model development: Senior Data Scientist develops price prediction models per commodity category: (a) features: (i) commodity price indices (lagged 0–6 months), (ii) FX rate, (iii) seasonal demand indicators, (iv) vendor-specific pricing history, (v) contract terms (volume commitments, payment terms); (b) models: gradient-boosted trees for short-term price prediction (1–6 month horizon); (c) output: predicted price range per SKU for next quarter with confidence interval; (d) backtesting: validate model on 2-year historical data — model must predict actual prices within 5% MAPE
Responsible (R): Senior Data Scientist
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 6–8 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1571_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1571_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1571_Task7" name="Negotiation recommendation engine">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Negotiation recommendation engine: For each vendor negotiation event: (a) system generates a negotiation brief: (i) current price vs. predicted market price (is the vendor&#x27;s offer above or below market?), (ii) price trend: is this commodity trending up or down? (timing recommendation: lock in now if trending up, delay if trending down), (iii) vendor margin estimate: if vendor&#x27;s price is significantly above predicted cost + reasonable margin (15–25%), flag as negotiation opportunity, (iv) benchmark: compare vendor&#x27;s price to other vendors in same category (anonymized), (v) recommended target price with confidence level; (b) Category Manager receives brief 1 week before scheduled negotiation per W738
Responsible (R): System / Senior Data Scientist
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Automated per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1571_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1571_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1571_Task8" name="PO timing optimization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: PO timing optimization: For high-value commodities with volatile pricing: (a) system monitors real-time commodity prices and FX rates; (b) when price drops below predicted range (buying opportunity): alert Category Manager — &quot;Steel prices dropped 5% this week. Consider placing Q3 orders now before prices recover.&quot;; (c) when price rises above predicted range (wait signal): alert Category Manager — &quot;Copper prices up 8% this month. If not urgent, delay Q3 copper wire orders. Expected price correction in 4–6 weeks.&quot;; (d) Category Manager decides based on alert + current inventory position per W4 (if stock is low, may need to buy regardless of price signal)
Responsible (R): System / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Continuous monitoring</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1571_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1571_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1571_Task9" name="Model performance tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Model performance tracking: Monthly: (a) Senior Data Scientist tracks model prediction accuracy: predicted vs. actual prices for the past month; (b) negotiation outcome tracking: did Category Managers who followed recommendations achieve better prices than those who didn&#x27;t?; (c) savings estimation: total savings from AI-informed negotiations vs. baseline (prior year same-vendor pricing); (d) quarterly report to VP Merchandising and CFO
Responsible (R): Senior Data Scientist
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1571_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1571_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1571_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1571_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1571_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-332 (ensure controlled execution — AI/ML &amp; Automation (PA-30.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Senior Data Scientist</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
