    <bpmn:process id="W_W1572" name="W1572. Intelligent Document Processing for Vendor Invoice Automation, Receipt OCR &amp; GL Code Auto-Classification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor invoice received (email, paper scan, or vendor portal upload per W7); or monthly AP volume review showing manual processing bottleneck
Frequency: Continuous — ~8,500–9,500 vendor invoices/month; each invoice triggers IDP processing
Volume: ~102,000–114,000 invoices/year; ~70–75% merchandise invoices (3-way match per W7), ~25–30% non-PO/recurring invoices (2-way match per W7C)
Owner: Senior Data Scientist
Participants: Senior Data Scientist, AP Manager, AP Clerk, IT Integration Specialist, CFO, IDP Vendor
Source: workflow W1572 — Intelligent Document Processing for Vendor Invoice Automation, Receipt OCR &amp; GL Code Auto-Classification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1572_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1572_Lane1" name="Senior Data Scientist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1572_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1572_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1572_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1572_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1572_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1572_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1572_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1572_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1572_Start4" name="Vendor invoice received (email, paper scan, or vendor portal upload per W7); or monthly…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1572_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1572_Task5" name="IDP platform selection &amp; setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: IDP platform selection &amp; setup: (a) evaluate IDP vendors: (i) accuracy for Philippine invoices (BIR-registered format with VAT breakdown, withholding tax), (ii) support for multilingual invoices (English, Filipino, Chinese for import vendors), (iii) integration with ERP AP module per W7, (iv) handling of handwritten vs. printed invoices, (v) pricing model (per-page or per-invoice); (b) select vendor and configure: (i) train OCR model on BuildRight&#x27;s top 50 vendor invoice layouts (each vendor has unique invoice format), (ii) define extraction fields: vendor name, TIN, invoice number, invoice date, PO number, line item description, quantity, unit price, total amount, VAT amount, EWT amount, payment terms; (c) IT Integration Specialist connects IDP platform to ERP via API
Responsible (R): Senior Data Scientist / IT Integration Specialist / IDP Vendor
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 6–8 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1572_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1572_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1572_Task6" name="Invoice ingestion &amp; extraction">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Invoice ingestion &amp; extraction: For each incoming invoice: (a) ingestion: (i) email invoices: auto-forward AP email to IDP platform, (ii) paper invoices: scan at AP office, upload to IDP, (iii) vendor portal invoices: API pull from vendor portal per W705; (b) OCR extraction: IDP processes invoice and extracts all defined fields with confidence scores; (c) for confidence &gt; 95%: auto-accept extraction; for confidence 80–95%: flag for AP Clerk review; for confidence &lt; 80%: route to manual processing
Responsible (R): System / IDP Platform
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (2–3 min/invoice)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1572_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1572_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1572_Task7" name="3-way matching automation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: 3-way matching automation (for PO-based invoices): (a) system matches extracted PO number and line items to purchase order in ERP: (i) quantity match: invoice quantity ≤ PO quantity (within tolerance ±5%), (ii) price match: invoice unit price ≤ PO unit price (within tolerance ±2%), (iii) GR match: goods receipt exists in ERP for the PO quantity; (b) if all three match: auto-approve for payment scheduling per W7; (c) if mismatch: generate exception report with discrepancy details for AP Clerk investigation
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): AP Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1572_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1572_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1572_Task8" name="GL auto-classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: GL auto-classification (for non-PO invoices): ML model classifies non-PO invoices: (a) features: vendor name, invoice description text, amount, historical GL coding for same vendor; (b) predict: GL account, cost center, tax code (VAT, EWT category); (c) model trained on 2 years of historical non-PO invoice coding; (d) for confidence &gt; 90%: auto-classify; for confidence &lt; 90%: route to AP Clerk with model prediction as suggestion; (e) AP Clerk corrections feed back to model for continuous learning
Responsible (R): System / ML Model / AP Clerk
Accountable (A): AP Manager
Duration: Automated + 1 min review for low-confidence</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1572_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1572_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1572_Task9" name="Continuous improvement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Continuous improvement: Monthly: (a) Senior Data Scientist monitors IDP performance: (i) extraction accuracy by vendor (track accuracy degradation for new vendor formats), (ii) 3-way match auto-approval rate (target: &gt; 70% auto-matched, &lt; 30% exceptions), (iii) GL classification accuracy, (iv) AP Clerk correction rate (corrections indicate model errors); (b) retrain GL classification model quarterly with corrected data; (c) add new vendor layouts when new vendors are onboarded per W34; (d) quarterly report to CFO: (i) invoices processed by IDP vs. manual, (ii) processing time reduction, (iii) error rate reduction, (iv) estimated annual cost savings (AP Clerk time × hourly rate)
Responsible (R): Senior Data Scientist / AP Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1572_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1572_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1572_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1572_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1572_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-332 (ensure controlled execution — AI/ML &amp; Automation (PA-30.2).) | - operational: per W51 to upskill AP Clerks for exception investigation
Owner: Senior Data Scientist</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
